      {
        "id": 38987,
        "name": "awp832",
        "username": "awp832",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/a9a28c/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-09-23T02:07:32.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>&nbsp;The first part you have right.&nbsp; The damage can be increased, decreased, redirected, etc, etc, etc...</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The second part is actually a really good question.&nbsp; I'm not sure on the answer here.&nbsp; I'm inclined to say that you'd have to trash the card.&nbsp;&nbsp; Not dealing the damage in the first place is different from dealing the damage and then having it be redirected or prevented by damage immunity.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>A few other cards, like Sonic Mine, or Ensnaring Brambles would have similar effects.</p>",
